  "text_md": "<!-- image -->\n\n## 718 Michael R. Douglas and Cristofero Fraser-Taliente\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n1000 initial states randomly scrambled between 1000-10000 times. We report results with a ball radius R = 5. and no T-calibration. For beam width 27 Or greater, we are able to solve all states.\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nFigure 2: Average solution length We find a best fit given by E = 1.92, where B is the beam width (trivially related to the number of nodes) . Excesses are always even due to parity. We report results with a ball radius R = 5, and no T-calibration.\n\n<!-- image -->",
